# SmartFilterBar for list module filters

Any **module list / directory toolbar** with search and/or quick filters MUST use `SmartFilterBar` — never a one-off `setTimeout` search row, ad-hoc `moduleFilterBar` markup, or a Search/Apply button.

Primitives: `src/components/filters/SmartFilterBar.tsx`, `smart-filter-types.ts`, `src/hooks/useDebouncedValue.ts`  
Shared i18n: `common.smartFilter.*` (reset, chips, active count, result count, **all**)  
Page-specific placeholders stay in the module namespace (`equipment`, `org`, `personnel`, …).

## Adopted modules (do not regress)

Assets, Org Designer tree, Admin Users, Work Orders, DI/Requests, Personnel, Inventory (master / topology / stock).

**Later pass (still use SmartFilterBar when touching them):** PM, Planning, Reliability pickers, Reference manager browser.

## Required path

1. Page owns values + side effects (Zustand / local state / IPC). SmartFilterBar never calls IPC or stores.
2. Wire `<SmartFilterBar searchValue … onSearchChange … filters={…} onReset={…} />`.
3. Search: debounce is **inside** the bar (300ms via `useDebouncedValue`). Use `onSearchChange` for settled query → store/load. Optionally `onSearchInputChange` to keep parent `searchValue` in sync.
4. Filters: `kind: "select" | "multi-select"` — apply **immediately** in each def’s `onChange`.
5. Reset clears search + filters in the **page adapter** (`onReset`); bar shows chips / active count.
6. **No new URL query sync** in the bar. Preserve existing DI `review`/`triage` presets in the page adapter only. Future `syncToUrl` belongs in the page, not SmartFilterBar props.
7. **“All” option label:** use the shared short label only — `common.smartFilter.all` (`Tous` / `All`). Omit `allLabel` so SmartFilterBar’s default applies, or pass `t("smartFilter.all", { ns: "common" })`. Never use long phrases such as “Toutes les familles”, “All warehouses”, “Tous les magasins”.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — local debounce + custom filter chrome
const t = setTimeout(() => setFilter({ search: q }), 300);
<div className={mfLayout.moduleFilterBar}>
  <Input … /><Button>Search</Button><Select … />
</div>

// ❌ BAD — long “all” labels
allLabel: t("filters.allFamilies") // "Toutes les familles"

// ✅ GOOD
<SmartFilterBar
  searchPlaceholder={t("filters.searchPlaceholder")}
  searchValue={searchInput}
  onSearchInputChange={setSearchInput}
  onSearchChange={(q) => { setFilter({ search: q.trim() || null }); void load(); }}
  filters={filterDefs} // select filters: omit allLabel → common.smartFilter.all
  resultCount={total}
  onReset={resetFilters}
/>
```

## Hard rules

- No Search/Apply button for text search.
- Do not reintroduce per-page `setTimeout(…, 300)` search debouncing.
- Do not put URL sync props on SmartFilterBar.
- Reuse `mfLayout.moduleFilterBar` / `mfInput.filterSearch` only **through** SmartFilterBar (or keep layout tokens elsewhere); do not fork a parallel filter chrome.
- Reference-backed **form** fields still use `ReferenceCombobox` (separate rule); SmartFilterBar is for list toolbars, not reference CRUD.
- Select filter "all" option must display **Tous** / **All** via `common.smartFilter.all` — not "Toutes les …" / "All families"-style phrases.
